<p>SCP-1130-1 is not visible to those not making use of directions dispensed by SCP-1130.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I find it odd that it can be photographed and recorded, and then seen by those viewing said photograph or recording regardless as to whether or not they were following the directions. It just counteracts what you're going for in my mind.</p>
<p>On a second note, I'm not too crazy about the transcript, either. The dialogue seems scripted at best, and as Smapti mentioned, it has that &quot;All D-Class Are Rugged Swearing Sailors&quot; quality to it. It doesn't really flow or sound natural. Otherwise, I do like it, and I think the description of the locations are interesting, but the dialogue prevents me from really enjoying it.</p>
<p>Otherwise, upvoted.</p>

