			<div class="content" id="post-content-1465865">
									

<p>I think this is good, reminds me of a lot of the older SCPs. There are things that could be improved on.</p>
<ul>
<li>I like the idea of the door only appearing to those following the map, but I think it would be better if it appeared to everyone, but no one other than those following the map would be able to enter it. There are physics problems to deal with in terms of objects only appearing to certain people, and it looks quite odd when a person walks right through a wall.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>I instantly start disliking anything what-makes-people-crazy in order to have a fear factor. Whatever lies inside the SCP's effect should cause natural psychological damage, which is much more terrifying than the current idea. If the thing in the SCP made the D-class in the transcript remove all his teeth willingly (I think it was to placate whatever was following him in there.), I would definitely be scared of venturing inside.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>In regards to the transcript, it's main weakness at this point is that it slides between too many points of view. Tell the story from one viewpoint, whether it be the D Class audio log in journal form, a transcription of a video feed, or anything else you come up with. Check the logs for SCP-87 for examples on how to do one well.</li>
</ul>
<p>I upvoted, but see if you can work on this stuff.</p>

