<p>You're a little too wishy-washy on making that aspect clear in the description. I had no idea that the chattering was the main culprit of the psychosis. You shouldn't wait to the end to reveal the hook, and I would revise the language to make it clear that the psychological state of the victims of the SCP is not directly attributed to an effect of the object.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Subjects exhibit highly erratic and aggressive behavior upon emergence from SCP-1130-2, necessitating appropriate measures to ensure maximum test efficiency.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is what I'm talking about. You should include the words &quot;psychological trauma&quot; or something to that effect to prevent readers from thinking that the object drives people mad. Remember, it's not what you write, it's how it reads, and you shouldn't need to translate your article for someone to get the point.</p>

